WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.634
-So we mentioned,
obviously, already in the show

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:07.234
this sort of historic act
about marijuana,

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:10.501
and certainly at
the federal level.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:12.267
The question I guess is,
you know, it's actually not

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:13.601
that many people
who are affected by it,

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:15.834
but it's such a big step
in the right direction.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:19.133
What happens next, other than
just pressuring governors

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:20.534
to do the same
on the state level?

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:23.400
Is there -- Do you see
legislation in the future?

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.300
-Well, you know,
we've tried over the years,

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.634
but let me just start
with saying this.

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:33.300
I strongly believe -- and the
majority of Americans agree --

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.300
nobody should have to go to jail
for smoking weed, right?

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:42.501
Right? And so we start with
that, and then we are,

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:44.400
to your point, urging --
and the president has been

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.167
very clear.
We're urging governors

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:49.200
and states to take our lead
and pardon people

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.167
who've been criminalized
for possession of marijuana.

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:55.801
And ultimately, though,
as with so many issues,

00:00:55.801 --> 00:01:02.334
if Congress acts,
then there is a uniform approach

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:03.801
to this
and so many other issues.

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:04.868
But Congress needs to act.

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:07.834
We're 29 days away
from the midterms.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.334
Ask who you're voting for
where they stand on this,

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:13.300
and I encourage you to vote
accordingly.

